        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (1-4)^2 \\times \\dfrac{1}{12}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Evaluate [MATH: (1-4)^2 \\times \\dfrac{1}{12}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we perform the operation inside the parentheses:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (1 \u2212 4_(\u23df)_(\u2212 3))^{2} \u00d7 (1)/(12)|= (\u2212 3)^{2} \u00d7 (1)/(12)]</span></p><p>Next, we compute the exponents:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (\u2212 3)^{2}_(\u23df)_(9) \u00d7 (1)/(12)|= 9 \u00d7 (1)/(12)]</span></p><p>Finally, we multiply:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9 \u00d7 (1)/(12)|=; (9)/(1) \u00d7 (1)/(12)|=; (9 \u00d7 1)/(1 \u00d7 12)|=; (9)/(12)|=; (9 \u00f7 3)/(12 \u00f7 3)|=; (3)/(4)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we perform the operation inside the parentheses:\n\n[MATH: (1 \u2212 4_(\u23df)_(\u2212 3))^{2} \u00d7 (1)/(12)|= (\u2212 3)^{2} \u00d7 (1)/(12)]\n\nNext, we compute the exponents:\n\n[MATH: (\u2212 3)^{2}_(\u23df)_(9) \u00d7 (1)/(12)|= 9 \u00d7 (1)/(12)]\n\nFinally, we multiply:\n\n[MATH: 9 \u00d7 (1)/(12)|=; (9)/(1) \u00d7 (1)/(12)|=; (9 \u00d7 1)/(1 \u00d7 12)|=; (9)/(12)|=; (9 \u00f7 3)/(12 \u00f7 3)|=; (3)/(4)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (1-4)^2 \\times \\dfrac{1}{12}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we perform the operation inside the parentheses:\n\n[MATH: (1 \u2212 4_(\u23df)_(\u2212 3))^{2} \u00d7 (1)/(12)|= (\u2212 3)^{2} \u00d7 (1)/(12)]\n\nNext, we compute the exponents:\n\n[MATH: (\u2212 3)^{2}_(\u23df)_(9) \u00d7 (1)/(12)|= 9 \u00d7 (1)/(12)]\n\nFinally, we multiply:\n\n[MATH: 9 \u00d7 (1)/(12)|=; (9)/(1) \u00d7 (1)/(12)|=; (9 \u00d7 1)/(1 \u00d7 12)|=; (9)/(12)|=; (9 \u00f7 3)/(12 \u00f7 3)|=; (3)/(4)]"
      },
