          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, consider the expression inside the parenthesis:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 \u00f7 (\u2212 2)^{2}]</span></p><p>Applying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 \u00f7 (\u2212 2)^{2}|=; 5 \u00f7 4|=; (5)/(4)]</span></p><p>Finally, we multiply:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (5 \u00f7 (\u2212 2)^{2}^(\u23de)^((5)/(4))) \u00d7 (\u2212 (4)/(5))|=; (5)/(4) \u00d7 (\u2212 (4)/(5))|=; \u2212 (5)/(4) \u00d7 (4)/(5)|=; \u2212 (5 \u00d7 4)/(4 \u00d7 5)|=; \u2212 (5 \u00d7 4)/(4 \u00d7 5)|=; \u2212 1]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, consider the expression inside the parenthesis:\n\n[MATH: 5 \u00f7 (\u2212 2)^{2}]\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n[MATH: 5 \u00f7 (\u2212 2)^{2}|=; 5 \u00f7 4|=; (5)/(4)]\n\nFinally, we multiply:\n\n[MATH: (5 \u00f7 (\u2212 2)^{2}^(\u23de)^((5)/(4))) \u00d7 (\u2212 (4)/(5))|=; (5)/(4) \u00d7 (\u2212 (4)/(5))|=; \u2212 (5)/(4) \u00d7 (4)/(5)|=; \u2212 (5 \u00d7 4)/(4 \u00d7 5)|=; \u2212 (5 \u00d7 4)/(4 \u00d7 5)|=; \u2212 1]",
